%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
Sitting in the corner with her arms around her knees,\nMitoko made a barely perceptible nod in the dark.%K%P
在黑暗中，抱着双膝的美都子的头、\n微微地点了一下，这并没有被我看漏。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDon't move from there. I wouldn't want you to cut\nyourself.\d%K%P
「在那儿不要动。\n可不能受伤啊」%K%P
I observed the leftovers we bought earlier today as they\nlay scattered across the upside-down dining table among\nall the shattered plates and cups.%K%P
翻倒的桌子的周围，\n是我们买齐的食材的悲惨遗体，\n还有打破的盘子和杯子的碎片，被撒得乱七八糟。\n打开垃圾袋，首先把大的碎片放进去。%K%P
I grabbed a couple of garbage bags and began to collect\nthe bigger fragments in one, and stuffed what was formerly\na luxurious feast into the other.%K%P
然后，打开另一个垃圾袋，\n把几个小时前还是佳肴的东西，全部倒了进去。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
After taking care of everything I could pick up by hand, I\nvacuumed the floor to get rid of any small bits of glass\nthat might have remained.%K%P
收拾完能用手捡起的碎片和食材，\n这次用吸尘器吸起了小块的碎片。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
Finally, I wiped up all traces of the sauce that had\nsplattered across on the floor.%K%P
最后，仔细地用抹布擦干净在地板飞散的酱汁和佐料汁。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
Mitoko spent all that time with her head buried in her\nknees, completely silent and motionless.%K%P
在此之间，美都子只是把头埋在抱着的双膝之间，\n一动不动，同时一言不发。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOkay... I'm turning out the lights.\d%K%P
「那就…关掉了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
I could see her make a small nod under the light of the\nfluorescent lamp.%K%P
荧光灯的亮光之下…\n美都子的头，又一次轻轻地点了一下。%K%P
I seemed to have successfully guessed what she wanted this\ntime.%K%P
似乎只有现在，\n我才能正确地理解美都子到底正在想什么。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAll right...\d%K%P
「嘿…咻」%K%P
I sat down at the opposite end of the room with my back\nagainst the door.%K%P
在抱膝坐着的美都子的另一侧…\n我靠着关上的屋门，慢慢地坐了下来。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
I couldn't make her out in the freshly descended darkness.%K%P
刚刚恢复一片漆黑的房间之中。%K%P
The sound of her breathing was the only evidence of her\nstill being in the room with me.%K%P
看不到应该坐在我正前方的美都子，\n只是通过微弱的气息才认识到她的存在。%K%P
After a few moments of blinking, I could finally make out\nthe rough contours of her shape.%K%P
在这样的黑暗中凝视了数秒，\n小小的、真的是非常小的轮廓，才模模糊糊地在我的眼前浮现出来。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I'm sorry.\d%K%P
「…抱歉」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
I had finally found the person I had to address.%K%P
终于，看清了正在和我说话的人。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry, Mitoko.\d%K%P
「抱歉，美都子」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry.\d%K%P
「对不起」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
Mitoko would always loudly scold me whenever I tried to\napologize for something that wasn't my fault.%K%P
每当觉得不是我的错我还道歉的时候，\n美都子都会猛地斥责我『不要道歉！』。%K%P
In other words, her silent treatment here only confirmed\nmy guilt. I had hurt her deeply.%K%P
这个女孩并没有由于我的『对不起』而愤怒，\n那是因为我的罪过真的伤害到了她吧。%K%P
It was another manifestation of my cowardice -- firing off\nan apology first in order to test how she felt about the\nsituation.%K%P
所以，当不清楚她的心情的时候，\n我都会耍『总之还是先道歉』这种花招。%K%P
As much as it conflicted with how I wanted to talk with\nher, this habit of mine was something that developed over\nthe six months we'd spent together.%K%P
这是我和美都子一起生活了半年得出的心得，\n是本末倒置的、我们两人之间的沟通方式。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhere do I even start...\d%K%P
「该从哪儿…说起呢」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
