%LC理
\dPlease, Kaya.\d%K%P
「呐、夏夜小姐？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
After confirming that every single door from Room #1 to\nRoom #3 was closed, I decided to continue.%K%P
接下来，我在再次开口之前，\n依次仔细确认了１号室到３号室的门扉是否有好好地关上。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI don't doubt your initial reason for moving in. It\nreally might've been no more than that.\d%K%P
「的确…对你来说，来到这里的理由，\n一开始也许就是这种程度的事」%K%P
It all felt serious enough for me. Heck, the very idea\nmade my entire body itch in directionless embarrassment...\nbut that hardly mattered here.%K%P
虽然嘴上说的是『这种程度』，但对我来说，\n已经是享尽了身为男人的福气，身体都有些发痒了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWasn't it fun, though? I mean, living the simple life,\npartying every night with all the others...\d%K%P
「但是，你不开心吗？\n和大家一起喝酒作乐，过着有些颓废的生活」%K%P
Those guys barged into our rooms -- or forcibly pulled us\ninto theirs -- without caring about whether or not we were\nbusy.%K%P
不管这边到底有没有工作，\n大家都会时而钻进我这边的房间、\n时而把我带到对面的房间。%K%P
They had no money, yet there was always booze to drink,\nsnacks to eat, and video games to play.%K%P
明明应该是没有钱的，却不知从那儿弄到手的\n酒、下酒菜、还有…各种各样的游戏机。%K%P
Even when I spent most of the time complaining or trying\nto stave off drowsiness, I still participated in all their\nsilly games and laid-back parties.%K%P
一边发着牢骚、一边忍着睡意，\n最后还是沉迷在闲扯和对战格斗中，一直到天明。%K%P
Kaya never rejected their invitations, either. She had fun\nwith everyone even when I wasn't around -- or so Mr.\nRetired told me, at any rate.%K%P
夏夜小姐，也完全没有拒绝过大家的邀请。\n据老爷子说，在我不在的时候她也会陪着大家一起闹。%K%P
...Now that I thought about it, it didn't quite sound like\nthe healthiest lifestyle to lead, but... honestly, few\nthings could surpass the sheer amount of good times we all\nshared together.%K%P
…用语言表达的话——就算的确是非常颓废，\n但是，那个时候的欢乐，实在是难以取代。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWeren't you having fun?\nWeren't you enjoying the time you spent with Mitoko?\d%K%P
「过得、不开心吗？\n和美都子在一起的时间」%K%P
An outsider who knew little about the two would have no\ndoubt interpreted their usual interactions as Kaya poking\nfun at Mitoko, while the latter fumed.%K%P
夏夜小姐和美都子的对话，从开头来看，\n一直是美都子带着怒意，夏夜小姐调皮地捉弄着她。%K%P
The air between the two wasn't particularly amiable, but\nthey never seemed genuinely upset with each other. Rather,\nthey were enjoying their little feuds.%K%P
虽然不知为何两人之间酿出了一些难以接近的氛围，\n但这两个人绝不是互相讨厌，\n倒不如说是在享受着这激烈的拌嘴。%K%P
At times, I even entertained the idea that they actually\nliked each other quite a bit.%K%P
有的时候，虽然不明确理由，\n她们两人会在黄昏的时候呆在一起，\n也会让我产生『这两个人，关系也许其实挺不错的？』的想法。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dIt wasn't that bad... obviously.\d%K%P
「并不坏的。\n这是，当然的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dRight.\d%K%P
「是吧」%K%P
As such, I had no trouble believing that everything Kaya\nhad just said reflected her true feelings.%K%P
所以，夏夜小姐这微微漏出的话语，\n让我相信，这就是她的真心。%K%P
Even now, she still had a reason to stay.%K%P
夏夜小姐留在这里的理由，就算在现在，也是有的。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dIf I had to express it somehow, I'd say I do love Ms.\nLandlord... but then I also realized how her desire to\nmonopolize you upset me beyond words.\d%K%P
「房东小姐，如果让我说是喜欢还是讨厌的话，我是喜欢的。\n但是，独占了理君的那个姑娘，感觉讨厌了起来…」%K%P
Yet Kaya was ready to throw away everything she had built\nup over the past few months because of a single fight.%K%P
但是夏夜小姐，仅仅因为一次吵架，\n就要把好不容易才发芽的东西全部摘掉。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI'm sure she feels the same way about me. And I want to\nkeep you to myself anyway. I can't help it anymore.\d%K%P
「我觉得那个女孩，和我想的是一样的。\n说回来，我果然还是想独占理君」%K%P
Despite being passionate and emotional on the inside, Kaya\nwas nonetheless extremely quick to give up.%K%P
明明身体里隐藏着黏黏糊糊的内面，\n却跟往常一样，只有放弃是最快的。%K%P
However...%K%P
但是…%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dIn other words... we'll never return to how we used to\nbe.\d%K%P
「所以说…已经回不去了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's no good. You need to come back.\d%K%P
「不行，请回去」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dOsamu...?\d%K%P
「理…君？」%K%P
But this time, I wouldn't let her.\n...Even if I had to take a shameless stance.%K%P
只有这次，不能让她这么做。\n…哪怕是，强行地将自己的事情放着不管。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDon't make me repeat myself. If even you end up leaving,\nwho's going to look after Mitoko?\d%K%P
「不要让我再重复了。\n夏夜小姐不在了，\n到底谁来保护美都子？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dThat's... for her to worry about, isn't it?\d%K%P
「那只是…房东小姐的任性而已吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's still a problem that we're directly to blame for\ncausing. You admitted it yourself a minute ago, too.\d%K%P
「造成了这种任性，是我们的原因。\n夏夜小姐，不也承认了吗」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dB-But... but then... who will look after -you-?\d%K%P
「但、但是、但是啊…\n那样的话，谁来照顾理君呢？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dMe...?\d%K%P
「我…吗？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWhere are you going to live? Do you have any savings?\nWhat about job hunting? How on earth are you planning to\nlive from now on?\d%K%P
「住的地方呢？租金呢？工作呢？\n从明天开始，要怎么生活呢？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'll... figure something out.\d%K%P
「这种程度总会有办法的…」%K%P
After all, I was an adult approaching the tail end of my\ntwenties. I was still very much in my twenties, though.%K%P
再怎么说，我也是马上就要告别２字打头的年龄的、正值壮年的大人…\n不过现在还是２０多岁。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dLike hell you're gonna figure something out!\d%K%P
「这肯定不行的吧！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's awfully harsh of you...\d%K%P
「你说肯定不行，也…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI would have been fine knowing that Ms. Landlord was here\nto look after you, but if you leave now, you're done for!\d%K%P
「理君留在这里的话，\n还能照顾房东小姐，我也能安心…\n但是，现在的理君不是已经走投无路了嘛！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDo you really have that little faith in me?\d%K%P
「我就是这么不值得信赖吗？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dOr what, are you gonna go running back to your ex-wife?\nNo. That's the one thing I won't stand for. And Ms.\nLandlord won't ever let you do anything like that,\neither!\d%K%P
「啊，难道想回到原来的夫人那边去吗？\n不行。只有这个我不允许。\n房东小姐肯定也绝对不会允许的哦？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhy are you bringing -her- up now...?\d%K%P
「为什么要在这里提到她啊…」%K%P
Hearing that made me feel like I still had a shot at\nmaking up with Mitoko.%K%P
…光听她这么说的话，\n似乎她和美都子之间还是有着和好的余地啊。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dAh, Christ, I'm gonna lose sleep over this... Did Ms.\nLandlord really tell you to get out? I bet she's already\nregretting everything she said.\d%K%P
「啊啊不行啊，越来越不安了…\n房东小姐，真的说了要让理君出去了吗？\n明明绝对会非常后悔的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIf you don't believe me, why don't you ask her yourself?\d%K%P
「要是怀疑的话，向本人确认一下如何？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Hahh.\d%K%P
「………哈啊」%K%P
She simply wouldn't give in.\nAll I wanted was for the two to have a conversation.%K%P
不上钩吗。\n我本来以为，至少会有一个对话的机会的。%K%P
But... that was as far as my meddling would go.%K%P
既然如此…已经没有我介入的余地了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm leaving on Sunday.\nThat's what I promised Mitoko.\d%K%P
「这个星期天，我就要走了。\n我和美都子，已经约好了」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dOsamu...\d%K%P
「理君…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt would do a lot to quell my worries if you could make\namends with her before then.\d%K%P
「如果可以的话还是希望你和美都子搞好关系，\n那样我也能安心了」%K%P
Although it seemed like Kaya was now even more concerned\nabout my future.%K%P
虽然这么说，夏夜小姐那边\n似乎对我的未来有很大的不安。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWhy... did it have to come to this...?\d%K%P
「为什么…会变成这样呢」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry. This is all my fault.\d%K%P
「抱歉。\n都是我的错」%K%P
Indeed, it was my fault.%K%P
没错，是我的错。%K%P
I was the one who made Kaya live through this, even\nhurting Mitoko in the process. I was responsible for\ngetting myself evicted.%K%P
让夏夜小姐这么难过也是。\n让美都子受到伤害也是。\n我被赶出去也是。%K%P
And...%K%P
还有…%K%P
I had brought all this upon myself -- my suffering and\npain was of my own making.%K%P
现在，我会抱着这么沉痛的思绪，也是我的错。%K%P
.........%K%P
………%K%P
......%K%P
……%K%P
...%K%P
…%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dThanks for waiting.\nI borrowed a car... It'll be 9800 yen for 4 hours.\d%K%P
「久等了，车借到了～。\n４个小时９８００日元呢～」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dI bet it would've been half that price without the stupid\ntheatre troupe logo on the side.\d%K%P
「带着这么恶趣味的剧团ＬＯＧＯ的话，\n只付一半也没问题吧」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dAhaha, I'll let you get away with paying for gas this\ntime around. In exchange, you'll have to use these\nspeakers to advertise my play as we drive. It premieres\nnext month.\d%K%P
「啊哈哈，只有油钱还是饶了我吧。\n不过相对的，要在街道上做移动宣传了。\n实际上公演下个月就要来了啊」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dI didn't know you were writing scripts for pro\nwrestling...\d%K%P
「你啊，实际上在写职业摔跤的脚本吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm so sorry for making you all do this despite your oh\nso busy schedules...\d%K%P
「对不起大家。\n每天这么闲，却还要特意请你们帮忙」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dWell, at least your sarcastic quips have gotten better.\d%K%P
「你只有讽刺水平进步了呢」%K%P
Sunday had come before we knew it.%K%P
就、是如此，转眼间来到了周日。%K%P
The sun was bright up in the blue sky as the cool breeze\ncaressed our skin -- in other words, it was the perfect\nday for moving.%K%P
今天是一个良辰吉日，\n绝佳的搬家的好日子…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHm?\d%K%P
「嗯？」%K%P
I thought I just saw something.%K%P
刚才、的确…%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dWhat's going on, Laid-off?\d%K%P
「怎么了，失业的？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh? Ah... it's nothing.\d%K%P
「诶？啊啊，没，什么都没…」%K%P
I could've sworn I saw the door to Room #5 open for a\nsecond.%K%P
５号屋的房门…\n好像稍微打开了一点点？%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dAll right then, let's take care of this already. It'll\nprobably only take two trips with the amount of stuff you\nhave.\d%K%P
「那么，赶紧搞起来吧。\n怎么着都得把失业者的行李在两趟里搬完」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dI get the feeling you could carry everything all at once\nif you tried.\d%K%P
「要是小熊一个人搬的话一趟就能搬完的吧？」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dAnd you forget that you're talking to a frail guy who\ncan't even leave his room on the best of days.\d%K%P
「对于每天一步都没法迈出房门的虚弱体质的我，\n你这可真是够残酷的」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dExercising outside would be more healthy for you, I'd\nsay.\d%K%P
「我感觉你要锻炼肌肉的话还不如去外面锻炼」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Phew.\d%K%P
「…呼」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dHere you go, Laid-off.\nI got you some water.\d%K%P
「来啦、失业的。\n水，提来了喔」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dTh-Thank you very much.\nI just finished vacuuming my room.\d%K%P
「啊，非常感谢。\n我这边也正好刚用吸尘器打扫完」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\d...It only took fifteen minutes to return the room to how\nit was before you moved in.\d%K%P
「…仅仅１５分钟、\n就变成跟过去一样空了呢」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat said, I'm still leaving with more than I came with.\d%K%P
「就算这样，行李也有增加啦」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dWell, you did roll in here with a single bag and not much\nelse.\d%K%P
「嘛，当初狼狈地进来的时候，\n只拿了一个包呢」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIndeed I did.\d%K%P
「嗯…」%K%P
The first thing I bought after moving in was an extra\nlarge futon -- one I would actually fit in.%K%P
一开始进入这间公寓的时候买的——\n和我的身材相吻合的，特大号的被子。%K%P
That, and some daily necessities we picked out with Mitoko\nat a 100 yen shop.%K%P
在百元店，和美都子一起买齐的日用品。%K%P
My friendly neighbors also found a table and a closet for\nme over at the dumping ground.%K%P
同各位住客一起去大型垃圾处理场捡回来的——\n桌子和衣柜。%K%P
There was also an obviously new clock, as well as a CD\nplayer that Kaya brought with her one night and \dforgot\d\nin my room.%K%P
夏夜小姐拿进来，若无其事地『忘记』拿走的——\n显然是新品的钟表和音响。%K%P
Before I knew it, my possessions had gone from a single\nbag to a whole truck's worth of stuff.%K%P
本来可以装在一个包里的我的东西，\n不知何时，已经增加到了可以装满一辆轻型卡车的量。%K%P
And it wasn't just things I gained over the course of the\nyear.%K%P
但现在，并不单纯是收拾行李的问题。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, I think we can leave after I finish cleaning up. I\nshould be done in about thirty minutes, Yasunaga.\d%K%P
「嗯，这样的话打扫完就可以出发了。\n八须永君，３０分钟后拜托你了」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dGotcha.\d%K%P
「好喔～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, then.\d%K%P
「接下来」%K%P
%LC???
%LC？？？
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...Eh?\d%K%P
「…诶？」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dPhew...\d%K%P
「呼…」%K%P
I opened the shoddy-looking window to let in some of the\ncool autumn air from outside. As much ventilation the gaps\nin the walls provided, they couldn't compete with an\nactual window.%K%P
打开仍然关不严实的窗户，\n明显地变凉了许多的秋风，\n以比平时的穿堂风猛烈得多的气势吹了进来。%K%P
I wiped the window frame with a cloth, careful not to\nbrush any of the dust into the room.%K%P
至于我，则是一边注意着不让太多灰尘进入房间，\n一边用抹布抹向窗框。%K%P
Seeing how this was my first time cleaning the thing since\nmoving in, my cloth turned completely black after only a\nfew swipes.%K%P
因为入住以来从未打扫过这个死角，\n抹布已经是一片漆黑。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThere we go...\d%K%P
「嘿…咻」%K%P
Nonetheless, I continued cleaning this thirty-something-\nyear-old room like it was the last thing I'd do in this\nworld.%K%P
但是我，仍然像是怀着深仇大恨…\n或者说是怀着深深的感激，\n彻底地打磨着这间已有超过３０年历史的房间。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
I found my way here after Ms. Hinoka reignited my will to\nlive.%K%P
满怀着绝望的人生，\n被穗香小姐在这里拯救。%K%P
Then nearly fell into a pit of despair upon learning that\nit was all just a misunderstanding on my part. And I most\ncertainly would have, had I not found a new goal in my\nlife.%K%P
知道那只是我的一厢情愿后，再次陷入绝望。\n不过，仍然在这个地方找到了一点点的存在意义。%K%P
Fresh hope budded in my heart... and was crushed almost\nimmediately, making me flee in a panic.%K%P
终于，我的人生又有了新的希望。\n然后被干脆地击溃，又一次陷入了绝望，从这里逃了出去。%K%P
Yet the promise of a new beginning made me return.%K%P
但是，又发现了新的希望，回到了这里。%K%P
And as I repeated this cycle, the people I had already\ntreasured became even more important to me... to the\nextent I...%K%P
在这样的过程不断重复的时候，重要的人们，\n明明已经变得更加重要了的…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNow the other side...\d%K%P
「接下来是另一侧…」%K%P
Yet here I was, about to return to my old life with only a\nsingle bag to my name.%K%P
现在，又要回到形影相吊的人生…了吗？%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dHere, have some tea.\d%K%P
「给，茶…」%K%P
%LC???
%LC？？？
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dSo... what is it, Mr. Retired?\d%K%P
「呃，在干什么呢…老爷子？」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dSlurp... Soon, the Young Master shall be leaving us.\d%K%P
「（呼）…差不多要走了呢，小少爷」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...\d%K%P
「唔…」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dMakes me wonder how he's going to live starting tomorrow,\nwith no money, job, or any prospect of survival.\d%K%P
「本来就是没有钱、没有职业也没有志气的一无所有的人啊。\n从明天开始，到底要怎样生活呢」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
